WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.112
Unit 2 is the guide's Step 4,
the web application firewall.

2
00:00:04.112 --> 00:00:08.668
Azure W A F runs in two places:
on Front Door, which is global,

3
00:00:08.668 --> 00:00:13.612
and on Application Gateway W A F
version two, which is regional.

4
00:00:13.612 --> 00:00:17.763
Either way it's a policy of managed
rules, custom rules and settings.

5
00:00:17.763 --> 00:00:20.550
Front Door's managed rules
need the Premium tier.

6
00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:25.937
Microsoft's Azure network security Zero
Trust recommendations check the same things

7
00:00:25.937 --> 00:00:30.725
on both: prevention mode, request body
inspection, the default rule set, the bot

8
00:00:30.725 --> 00:00:35.888
protection rule set, rate limiting, a
JavaScript challenge, and diagnostic logging.

9
00:00:35.888 --> 00:00:39.595
Application Gateway adds
the H T T P DDoS rule set;

10
00:00:39.595 --> 00:00:42.375
Front Door adds a CAPTCHA challenge.

11
00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:45.584
The Zero Trust Assessment
automates these checks,

12
00:00:45.584 --> 00:00:48.620
so a policy that misses
one shows up as a finding.
